{
  "id": "merge-two-level",
  "title": "A survivor is itself merged later (flattening and the convergence projection)",
  "covers": [
    "ticket follow-up 1: convergence = live rows + merged_into_id",
    "merge: merged_into_id is never a chain",
    "merge: a re-match that lands on an existing note merges"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "W studies 食べる, M studies 持つ. B's duplicate L1 of 持つ is merged into M (seq 4).",
    "A re-matches M to 食べる (entry_seq register, T+20). That collides with W, so M is merged into W (seq 6). L1.merged_into_id is re-pointed from M to W: never a chain.",
    "B, still offline, tags L1 at T+30. On the server this arrives after both merges and is applied to L1 and forwarded to W - not to M.",
    "On phone B the same edit was applied BEFORE the merges, so there it travelled L1 -> M -> W, and B's copy of M has tags = [late] while the server's copy of M has none.",
    "That difference is allowed: rows with merged_into_id set are compared only on (id, merged_into_id, deleted_at). W, the live row, is identical everywhere.",
    "B's last op changes L1.entry_seq (T+31): entry_seq is never forwarded and does not un-merge."
  ],
